tmp_text "My opionion: To get our best weapons(Katana and Wakizashi) is really too hard.But I thinkthats ok.If you want best weapon,you must fight.But If you died and you lostyour Wak. or Katana it is too much for me(us).So try to think what to do with it. I thin k if we died and concentrate on Susanoo, He could get us our lost weapon (Katana or Wakizashi).   Bye         Susanoo**I would like to know whats the matter with darts. I didn't see them in the shop for a long time.What the hell is it?.How we can use our poison ? * GRIN * ****My suggestion is this:-If you die and drop your wak as a result then your wak disappears, and the loss is registered. When you go to the jingu and concentrate on Susano-o,then Susano-o gives your wakizashi/katana back to you. Also, as far as questsgo then maybe something a little more elegant than lockers. How about youhave to give your weapon to the Shogun while you do the quest (ie put itinto his care) However in that case I think it would be kinda neat if he won'treturn it till the quest is done (ie you say something about care, and he)asks what quest it is for, so you tell him, he accepts the wak and returnsit to you if you go in there and say \"quest done\" and you have indeed finished the quest) This means that you only lose the weapon from when you need to lose it to the beginning of the quest. Of course it would requirea little maintenance from a wiz to make sure that any new quests whereplayers do have to drop their weapons are noted so that the Shogun can accept for them. I don;t know how difficult this would be to code, but I'dbe happy to help any other wizzes who have more time to work on it.Dazza**Some people play this mud just to hack and slash everything in sight.  But me,I use this mud as a cheap phone call to my girlfriend in real life (whenevershe is on) and a bit of roll playing - I get into the ninja character and myAxl character pretty well I think.  Yes, it would be a great idea to removeour weapons and place them into someone's care as we do a quest or something.A while back, I was talking to Exos about his samaurai guild and the possib-ilities of little fueds between the two guilds - the honorable samaurai withtheir katana and wakizashi versus the stealthy ninja with our ninja-to.  Someof the ideas were they had objects lying around and we stole them and theycame back to retrieve them, etc. etc.  Takes away from the same old killmonster, reset, kill monster, etc.  A bit of roll playing...what I am gettingat is just because we give our weapon to our Shogun (a flaky dude that doesnot say too much) does not mean we will automatically get them back.  Maybethey were stolen or misplaced - here is an idea.  If a wizard would like topair up with me and maybe a few others, create a rival ninja clan to our eastof the island - put their guild out in the water and a secret path that leadsto them or something.  Have a bunch of multi-leveled ninja, su-jen, maybe evenanother Shogun out there with our stolen weapon; meaning we would have toutilize other weapons, which we should be able to do already (along with abunch more that can be coded for our purposes).  In a sense, we have no truerival guilds in this mud, so maybe we can have a NPC guild against us.  Andmaybe if we take too long to retrieve our stolen weapons, they were sold offinto the Yakuza *grin*>>>>>Axlrose - just popping off some ideas off the top of his head<<<<<**I was thinking along just the same lines actually - scarey I know!No more elboration for now - till I know a bit moreabout the coding - I'm very much a newbie wiz at the moBut you and I are thinking along same lines(autoloading weapons for game balnce should be a bastard)sorry to piss opn the other ninjas' bonfires but Axls ideais probably better for game balanceDazza the drunk (but not stoned for at least 2 more days ;))**Darts are usually in the guild shop (w w n) but there have been a lack ofthem lately... i only could get 3 this afternoon when i was making poisondarts.... maybe it had something to do with the reboot being cancelled or maybe other ninja's had them.  On a simular note to all ninja's please be considerate to the newbiesespecially... sell all guild materials in the guild shop... don't sellthem around the mud.Just my opinions on things.... 	the loving the revitalization of the guild                                  labarum**I don't know what's happening about darts - if any other wizzes have any ideaplease let me knowDazza**I overheard talk of changes to our guild.  I also saw something in one of these notes regarding them.  Could someone pots/mail me a listof these changes?TURBO**hiGambit told me when he dies he looses the katana and the wakazashi.This was because there was an old problem, that an autoload objectwhich is dropable can be doubled by a clever player :*)because:1 step: auto_load() playerfile2 step: drop()... but before the drop comes the playerfile is saved so that from droping the katana was still auto_load ... Now recoded that file so that you get the katana after death, its still autoload and you candrop and get it , which the old idea was :)         So thanks to Gambit which told me that problem :)                    whisky the Gnome**o.k. i have been lost on this subject from the starti was told all you had to do was put the blood into the eggand it would work.  Guess what? it don't work.how does the egg/poison making process start/middle/end?			confused,				DF**Say egg to shogun - he'll fill you inDazza**increased the damage of assassinate, so that it is a feature again andnot such a punny thing it'd been lately.the change to hit with assassinate depends on yer skill, the damage yedo on yer dex (so get yer dex up ! *grin*)enjoy it                                Pat, the evil bat (pet)**Just one question: Is the new assasination as deadly as before?(For monster and for u us)Thanks :-)**check it out                 pat**1)WELCOME TO THE BEST GUILD IN THE GAME2)read all help files before you try to do anything it will solve most questions3)Weapons: use only ninja weapons it's better for your character in the long run4)don't sell ninja stuff outside the guild5)read help weapon file to find out what you can and can not wield.6) have fun and good luck****"
